<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2016/Evening.jpg" alt="An abstract, impressionistic painting of the sunset" data-filename="Sunrise.JPG" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Sunrise. 8x6, oil on linen panel. 2016</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This sketch was started using an oil stick to do the basic block in of the darks. Today was the first time I've tried using one and I was instantly addicted: I immediately started three other paintings.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">What I've tried to do here is to make the painting about the light in the atmosphere. There isn't a careful painting of subject matter, and the identity of most of the things in the foreground has been left up to the viewer to determine. When I tried to do this as a close rendering of the scene, the result didn't have nearly as much impact; time and time again, I've found out that light in the sky is more effective when done as a simple smear of paint.</p>
